  "date": "2026-10-25",
  "scope": "Actual recovered catalog root/candidate scan through exact resolved JSON mark, durable append and complete pending snapshot. Native lock/descriptor/namespace/BatchIo and logical closure/progress correspondence remain open.",
  "runtime_changes": "Catalog::collect_with_stat calls gc_mark::mark before its existing fault boundary and batch. Already normalized catalog keys are encoded with path_encoding=1; resolver lexical validation remains. Redundant path normalization is removed, candidate array order is unspecified, format and barrier count are unchanged. No performance campaign or speed guarantee.",
  "properties": {
    "gc_mark::snapshot": "The executable HashSet-to-Vec loop enumerates exactly all input keys.",
    "gc_mark::event": "Executable construction emits exactly the supplied deleted paths and path_encoding=1, with no other fields.",
    "gc_mark::{mark_fold,wire_marks,append_marks}": "Ordered actual decoded mark operations update exactly tombstones and pending; the typed fold agrees with the exact input event and confirmed log history.",
    "gc_mark::mark": "Actual owner-root/candidate methods compose with JSON event, catalog_append and pending enumeration. Every eligible candidate is marked; old pending survives; previously receipted tombstones are not reintroduced. Owners/packs/edges/handoff receipts remain unchanged. Nonempty success confirms one durable frame; empty candidates perform no mark I/O. No target batch is returned on failure.",
    "catalog_append::append": "Strengthened erased contract exposes write-failure quarantine and pre-write state-error preservation."
  },
  "trusted_boundaries": [
    "Two added external serde_json primitive contracts: empty Map::new and exact Number::from(u64). The audited whitelist now contains 17 primitives; no admitted straw body.",
    "Existing Writer, Resolver, KeySet, JSON encode/parse observations and String identity/order/hash laws. Initial log valid/ready/interpreted preconditions are explicit.",
    "Actual locked refresh and fd binding, canonical recovered identities, full queue/reader/checkpoint/publication roots and closure/cache remain native caller obligations.",
    "BatchIo target/path/parent/repair/receipt conformance and aggregate batch projection remain unproved. No unconditional or end-to-end GC liveness claim."
  ],
